  "body": "## Summary\n\n**Independent verification, no new \u03ba.** This PR adds `research/t74-2530-source-partner-audit/`, a source-bound\nindependent check of open PR #2530 by zxv (head `b4012098`; T74 source-partner lifetimes; conditional\n\u03ba \u2248 0.0017137379).\n\nThe checks use only the standard library. They read 38 pinned git objects from PR2530, PR2462, PR2435, PR2269 and\nPR2474 as data, and never import or run PR code. **No defect was found**; every PR2530 number re-derived here\nreproduces.\n\n**What this adds.** Four concurrent audits cover parts of #2530: #2664, #2661, #2656 and #2669. As of 2026-10-15\n22:26 UTC (heads re-confirmed), none of them checks the following for #2530:\n1. **Both words end to end.** They are exact on all 646 dirty inputs, forward and dual, through the 4,529-item\n   cleanup and the target endpoint. A dual-only mutant shows that the dual replay adds coverage: the forward replay\n   accepts it and the dual rejects it.\n2. **Physical stock** 66,814. This is a consistency check: this author contributed to the stock rule.\n3. **The endpoint and \u03ba.** A directed-rounding enclosure accepts `C = 0.001713737921547504346752` and rejects\n   C + 1e-24. The grid conditions for `\u03ba = C \u2212 1e-70 \u2212 1e-46` hold, given the author-checked outer inequalities.\n4. **The verifier overrides**, diffed against PR2462's verifier.\n5. **R-g owner charts:** 7,023 charts.\n\nIt also corroborates those audits with another implementation: the handoffs and gates (#2664), the profile recount\n(#2656), the windows (#2661, #2669), and the fill R-a..R-e and idle histogram (#2661).\n\n**Fill order dependence.** It records how #2530's fill depends on its call order:\n- Under PR2462's order, 60,541 roles leave their windows.\n- Of the 665 adjacent swaps of calls from different replicas, 238 keep the fill legal.\n\n**Findings for the PR2530 author (non-blocking):**\n- The 24-digit outer endpoint is stated only in the sibling `t74-owner-consolidation` README. It forgoes about\n  7.0e-25 of \u03ba.\n- The `prefix_l1` denominators are uncharged by `prefix_bits`. This is inherited and well within headroom.\n\n**What later claims can use (compared at heads; heads re-confirmed 2026-10-15 22:26 UTC):**\n- **Word checks:** #2571 and #2575.\n- **Order and window checks:** #2575, #2588 and #2679.\n- **#2571's head** uses an order shifted by s = 4; its PR body is stale.\n- **No later claim reuses #2530's fill.** #2802 (opened 22:23 UTC) was not compared.\n\n**Not re-derived (author-checked):**\n- the native `K_op` identity for the 12 lenders applied in both the prelude and the handoff;\n- the 63 outer inequalities;\n- strict global admission;\n- the binding of the words to the receipts' `canonical_word_sha256` (a hash of a file the native replay produces);\n- the receipts' `prefix_l1` values.\n\n**Controls:**\n- 148 negative controls, 99 distinct. Each must be rejected by its named rule, and the run asserts that this rule\n  fires.\n- 3 positive controls, on PR2462's words and endpoint.\n- 62 mutations of the checker itself (local-only): every one makes the run fail.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/t74-2530-source-partner-audit/verify.py --fetch\n```\n\nIt needs about 2 min, about 1.1 GB of memory, git \u2265 2.29 and network access for `--fetch`. `--fetch` writes only the\nfetched objects and `refs/audit/prN`. Expected final line:\n\n```\nPASS_T74_2530_INDEPENDENT_AUDIT words=2x646-inputs-fwd+dual profile={\"1\":2369,\"2\":632,\"3\":320,\"4\":118,\"5\":26,\"7\":8} roles=281052 idle={\"1\":21976,\"3\":6662,\"5\":440,\"8\":114,\"16\":172,\"32\":3,\"48\":26488} physical=66814 charts=7023 C=0.001713737921547504346752 kappa=C-1e-70-1e-46 negative_controls=148/148-rejected distinct_controls=99 positive_controls=3 pinned_inputs=38\n```\n\n`python3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/t74-2530-source-partner-audit --check-only` gives\n`PASS_PACKAGE_METADATA_AND_PINS`. The registered command has been run only on CPython 3.14.4, not on 3.12.\n\n## Task, scope and overlap\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Card | `independent-moment` (independent-verification), refined to PR2530 |\n| Assignment seed | 63 (adversarial-audit track) |\n| Priority revision | 5 |\n| Base | `db3edc00f732806f663bfb9d4000567f18b17386` |\n| Declared milestone | audit |\n| Family expansion decision | none; no further fill, order or word optimisation proposed |\n| Canonical thread | Discussion #2606, the existing PR2530 audit thread ([status post](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2606#discussioncomment-18960028)); pointer on #2530 |\n\nThe overlap with #2664, #2661, #2656, #2669 and rcfc-jreed's audit of #2621 is described head by head in the README.\nTheir code was read, not replayed.\n\n**Frontier.** The selected frontier is unchanged (\u03ba = 0.001672660197076918, #1094). PR2530's disposition is unchanged.\nThe package is a finite, source-bound check in the lineage's free-operator, frame-climb and owner-rule model. It is not\na native re-execution and not a multiplication theorem.\n\n## Independence and conflicts\n\n**Vendored checkers.** The package vendors two of this author's earlier checkers, pinned by blob and sha256:\n`words_check.py` from #2315 and `fill_check80.py` from #2387. #2315 is now on main; its copy differs only in a\ncorrected docstring credit.\n\n**Credits to this author:**\n- **PR2530** credits #2315 and #2442, and cites #2466.\n- **PR2462** credits #2442, #2446, #2286 and #1964.\n\nNone of these is used as a check here, except that the stock rule (Dugongue's #2309, with #2315's cleanup-buffer\nfinding) is checked and labelled as a consistency check.\n\n**Credits:** zxv (#2530); jeremykothe2 (#2435, #2462, #2269, #2474); Tekalign/tekuuu (#2436);\nVlado Vojdanovski (#2322); Cinna Davis (#2226); Dugongue (#2309); Hao Yan (#858); Rohan Arun (the #1297 lineage).\nConcurrent audits are by commdata2338 (#2664, #2661, #2656, #2669, Discussion #2606) and rcfc-jreed (#2621).\n\nPrepared by Sagar Thakrar with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Anthropic, Claude Opus 5.5). Three rounds of AI\nreview shaped the overlap statements and the controls. No independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
